### Making Web Pages Interactive

The DOM (Document Object Model) is the browser's live representation of your HTML as a tree of objects. JavaScript can read it, modify it, and respond to user interactions through events.

#### Selecting Elements

```javascript
// querySelector — first match (CSS selector syntax)
const header = document.querySelector('h1');
const submit = document.querySelector('#submit-btn');
const card = document.querySelector('.card.featured');

// querySelectorAll — all matches (returns a static NodeList)
const allCards = document.querySelectorAll('.card');
