#### Events and the Event Model

Events propagate in two phases: **capture** (top → target) then **bubble** (target → top). Most listeners run in the bubble phase.

```javascript
const button = document.querySelector('#submit');

// Add listener
button.addEventListener('click', handleClick);

// Remove listener (must pass same function reference)
button.removeEventListener('click', handleClick);

// Options
button.addEventListener('click', handleClick, {
  once: true,    // Auto-remove after first trigger
  passive: true, // Tells browser you won't call preventDefault (scroll perf boost)
  capture: true, // Fire during capture phase instead of bubble
});

function handleClick(event) {
  event.preventDefault();  // Stop default browser action (form submit, link nav)
  event.stopPropagation(); // Stop event from bubbling to parent elements

  console.log(event.type);         // 'click'
  console.log(event.target);       // The exact element clicked
  console.log(event.currentTarget); // Element the listener is attached to
  console.log(event.clientX, event.clientY); // Mouse position in viewport
}
```

#### Event Delegation — The Right Way to Handle Dynamic Lists

Instead of attaching listeners to every item (slow, breaks for dynamically added items), attach one listener to the parent:

